# half(list[k]): the element goes from the bytes into the floating-point register of the argument, and the result is added as it comes back. Nothing is boxed.
# The bytes may hold a NaN of any bits and a parameter holds only one kind of NaN, so the element is compared with itself ahead of the call. A NaN takes a rare arm.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 1
# HOT: Double b@[[sum]] = Phi(
# HOT: Double b@[[element]] = Load(b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:GetTypedArrayElement)
# HOT: Int32 b@[[isNumber]] = Equal(b@[[element]], b@[[element]], {{*}}:CallDirect)
# HOT-NEXT: Branch(b@[[isNumber]], Terminal, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# HOT-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#{{*}}
# HOT: Double b@[[half]] = Patchpoint(b@[[element]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ControlDependent, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# HOT-NEXT: Double b@{{*}} = Add(b@[[sum]], b@[[half]], {{*}}:Add)
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# The length and the address of the bytes are not read again behind the call, which cannot change them.
# NONE-LABEL: steps by 1
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSArrayBufferView
# NONE-NOT: ExitsSideways
# NONE-LABEL: end of loop
